  "theory": {
        "intro": "To **evaluate** a power, write it in expanded form and multiply the factors together.",
        "facts": [
          "$3^{2}=3\\times 3=9$ and $2^{5}=2\\times 2\\times 2\\times 2\\times 2=32$.",
          "An index of $1$ leaves the number unchanged: $412^{1}=412$.",
          "$1$ to any index is $1$, and $0$ to any index of $1$ or more is $0$.",
          "A power of $10$ is a $1$ followed by that many zeros, so $10^{4}=10\\,000$.",
          "$10^{6}$ is one million and $10^{9}$ is one billion."
        ],
        "steps": [
          "Write the power in expanded form.",
          "Multiply the factors together, working from left to right."
        ]
      },
